# Unsafe code allow-list for soroban-zk-std workspace
#
# Every `unsafe` block in this workspace must appear in one of the files listed
# here.  The CI step `unsafe-audit` runs `grep -rn "unsafe" crates/` and fails
# the build if any match falls outside these paths.
#
# Adding a new file to this list requires a companion PR comment explaining:
#   1. Why safe Rust cannot achieve the same goal.
#   2. The invariant the unsafe code relies on (mirrors the // SAFETY: comment).
#   3. Which reviewer approved the addition.
#
# ── Allowed files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Volatile zero-fill of sensitive stack buffers.
# Invariant: write_volatile through *mut u8 at a valid, aligned T prevents
# dead-store elimination of the zero-fill without requiring the `zeroize` crate.
crates/soroban-zk-core/src/zeroize.rs

# GlobalAlloc impl for the allocation-counting test allocator.
# Invariant: delegates entirely to System; counter logic does not affect
# the returned pointer or heap layout.
crates/soroban-zk-core/tests/plonk_no_alloc.rs
